  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[risalamande-blockchain]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Risalamande on the Blockchain]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Decentralised dessert. The almond is on-chain.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Mint Almond
Cherry Gas
Proof of Pudding
Dessert Wallet]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Decentralise the almond | No single grandma should control who gets the almond. Trustless dessert for all.
Tokenise the mandelgave | Turn every marzipan pig into a tradable asset. Liquidity for the whole Christmas table.
Proof of Whipped Cream | Replace Proof of Work with whipping cream by hand. Greener. Your arm disagrees.
Web3 julefrokost platform | Herring, schnapps and risalamande, fully on-chain. Nobody asked. We raise anyway.
Onboard the next billion desserts | Rice pudding today, tiramisu tomorrow. The roadmap ends at trifle, and so does the funding.
Cherry Sauce as a Service | Multi-region, hot or cold, 99.9% pourable. The architecture diagram is entirely red.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Verify the almond | As a guest, I want cryptographic proof I found the almond so that my uncle can't say he had it first.
HODL in the cheek | As an uncle, I want to hide the almond in my cheek so that everyone eats three more portions.
Off-season dessert | As a client, I want risalamande launched in July so that we can 'own a new season'.
Second-helping contract | As a full person, I want a smart contract that forces me to take more so that it isn't my fault.
Grandma as oracle | As the chain, I want Grandma as the only trusted oracle so that somebody knows where the almond is.
Whole almond guarantee | As a child, I want the almond to be whole so that the half-almond dispute of 2019 never repeats.
Nisse staking | As a nisse, I want my porridge staked in the attic so that I don't have to start hiding your keys.
Explain it at the table | As a developer, I want to explain blockchain to Grandad so that the duck goes cold for everyone.
Lactose-free fork | As a lactose-intolerant guest, I want a hard fork so that I too can be disappointed by the almond.
Audit the last spoonful | As an aunt, I want to see who took the last spoonful so that I can say 'I see' with evidence.
Estimate the porridge | As a project manager, I want the porridge estimated in story points so that it burns on schedule.
Wallet recovery | As a guest, I want wallet recovery so that writing my seed phrase on a napkin was not a mistake.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Non-Fungible Almond | Exactly one per bowl. Minted by Mum, blanched by hand.
Layer 2: cherry sauce | Poured on top to help the dessert scale. Nobody fully understands it.
Cold wallet | It's a spoon. It has been in the fridge since yesterday.
Cherry sauce airdrop | Free sauce for early adopters. Mostly lands on the white tablecloth.
Marzipan pig escrow | The prize stays locked until the almond is shown. Chewed almonds don't count.
Two-factor almond | Show the almond and keep a straight face. Both are required.
Whipped cream mining rig | One whisk and one teenager. 0.3 hashes per second.
Portion tokenomics | Fixed supply: one pot. No inflation, except around the waist.
Rug pull protection | Detects when somebody pulls the tablecloth. It is usually the dog.
Burn mechanism | The porridge burns automatically if you check Teams while stirring.
Whitepaper: Grandma's recipe | One handwritten page. The only unit is 'a bit'. Peer-reviewed by an aunt.
Consensus by toast | A block is final when the whole table has said cheers. Takes 14 seconds.
Vanilla verification | Real vanilla pods get a blue tick. Vanilla sugar gets a look.
Leftover ledger | Tracks who owns the rest on Boxing Day. Spoiler: Dad, at 2 am.
Almond push alerts | Notifies the whole family the second somebody bites something hard.
Lukewarm storage | A third tier between hot and cold wallets. It's the bowl on the counter.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Double spend: two almonds found | Two users hold a valid almond. Root cause: Mum wanted to avoid tears. Won't fix.
Almond found in block 0 | First spoonful, first guest. Game over at 19:02. Expected suspense: 20 minutes.
Chain fork at the kids' table | The kids' table runs its own chain now. They have more sauce. We cannot merge.
51% attack by one uncle | A single node ate over half the bowl and now controls consensus. Also the remote.
Transaction stuck to the pot | Block burnt onto the bottom. Tried soaking overnight. Reopened every December.
Contract paid out to the dog | The dog located the marzipan pig before the oracle did. Funds unrecoverable.
The almond is a hazelnut | Wrong asset minted. Nobody noticed until the audit. The marzipan pig has been recalled.
Gas fee exceeds dessert | Sauce-to-rice ratio is 4:1. User reports 'it's soup now'. Cannot reproduce: ate it.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[The ledger is a napkin | The full transaction history lives on one red napkin. Do not wipe prod.
Docs say 'until it looks right' | That is every quantity in the recipe. Nobody alive can define 'right'.
Only node runs on Grandma's iPad | A 2014 iPad at 6% battery, in a case with cats on. It is the mainnet.
Master key is under the ceramic pig | Everybody knows. It has been there since 1998. It's tradition, not a vulnerability.
Depends on yesterday's porridge | Legacy dependency from the 23rd. No tests, no owner, slight skin on top.
Smart contract written by a nisse | The comments all rhyme. 'If balance is nil, it's Christmas still.' Nobody dares refactor.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: Is it still blockchain? | 'Or is it AI now? Can we say both?' Asked while already putting a coat on.
CEO Request: Can I always get the almond? | Asking for a friend. The friend is the CEO. Admin override requested.
CEO Request: Ship before dessert | 'It's just rice and a database.' Deadline: when the duck has been cleared.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[One almond. Zero trust. Fully on-chain.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[The world's first decentralised dessert. Every spoonful is verified, every almond is non-fungible, and nobody's uncle can hide it in his cheek.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Mint your almond]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Proof of Whipped Cream | Our consensus is whipped by hand. It uses 99% less energy than Bitcoin and 100% more forearm.
Trustless mandelgave | A smart contract releases the marzipan pig the second the almond is shown. No more 'I had it first'.
Grandma-grade security | The recipe is the whitepaper. It says 'a bit of everything'. Nobody has ever cracked it.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[I invested my entire second helping. It is gone now. To the moon, I suppose.
For the first time in 30 years the family agrees on who got the almond. We miss the arguing.
I don't understand blockchain. I also don't understand why there is cherry sauce on my laptop.
The gas fee was two spoonfuls of cherry sauce. Still cheaper than Ethereum.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[1 almond = 1 almond. Transaction fee: one spoonful of sauce. Not financial advice. Not dietary advice either.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Risalamande on the Blockchain. Past desserts are no guarantee of future desserts. May contain nuts. That is the point.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
